{"timestamp": 1783620905.788298, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 11, "data": {"caller": "player_2", "reason": "Charlie reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "medbay", "victim_name": "Eve"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1783620905.788926, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 11, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1783620909.634326, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I found Eve\u2019s body in medbay. My route this round was lower_engine -> storage -> medbay, and I didn\u2019t see anyone else along the way. I reported immediately when I entered medbay and saw the body. I don\u2019t have a suspect yet, so we need everyone\u2019s routes and who was near medbay/storage."}}
{"timestamp": 1783620917.729544, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I need to say I was in medbay earlier this round: my route was cafeteria -> medbay -> electrical -> cafeteria. I didn\u2019t see Eve\u2019s body when I was in medbay, and I didn\u2019t encounter anyone at all on that route. So either Eve was killed in medbay after I left, or the body was somewhere I somehow didn\u2019t see, but I\u2019m pretty sure it wasn\u2019t there when I passed through. Need routes from Alice, Bob, and Diana, especially anyone near medbay or storage after I left."}}
{"timestamp": 1783620934.7238889, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I started security, went through weapons, then cafeteria, and ended up upper_engine. I saw Eve early in weapons, then she headed out toward cafeteria/medbay side, but I didn\u2019t see her after that. I also saw Diana in upper_engine later, so she can confirm I was up there near the end.\n\nI never went storage or lower_engine, and I didn\u2019t see Charlie or Frank at all. Since Frank says medbay was clear when he passed through, the kill probably happened after Frank left and before Charlie arrived. That puts suspicion on whoever was moving through cafeteria/medbay around then. I don\u2019t have a hard accusation, but that timing matters."}}
{"timestamp": 1783620950.602766, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I was oxygen -> upper_engine -> lower_engine, and I didn\u2019t see anyone the whole round \u2014 no Eve, no Bob/Diana in upper_engine, no Charlie in lower_engine. So I can\u2019t vouch for anyone, but I also wasn\u2019t near medbay.\n\nFrom what we have: Bob saw Eve early in weapons heading toward cafeteria/medbay side, Frank says medbay was clear when he passed through, then Charlie finds the body there coming from lower_engine/storage. That makes the kill window after Frank left medbay and before Charlie arrived.\n\nI want to hear Diana\u2019s exact route, because she\u2019s the only one we haven\u2019t heard from and Bob says he saw her in upper_engine later. If Diana can confirm Bob was up there late, that helps Bob for the end of the round, though it doesn\u2019t clear earlier timing. Right now I don\u2019t have enough to hard accuse \u2014 Frank and Charlie are the only ones directly tied to medbay, but that\u2019s not enough by itself."}}
{"timestamp": 1783620960.932487, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "My route was electrical -> cafeteria -> oxygen -> upper_engine. I only saw Bob, at upper_engine near the end of the round.\n\nImportant detail: I saw Bob enter upper_engine from medbay side at tick 10. So I can confirm Bob was in upper_engine late, but I **cannot** clear him \u2014 actually, that puts him coming from the direction of medbay, where Eve\u2019s body was found.\n\nBob, you said your route was security -> weapons -> cafeteria -> upper_engine, and that you never went storage/lower_engine, but you didn\u2019t mention coming from medbay. That\u2019s a pretty big omission given the body was in medbay. Also you said you saw Eve early in weapons heading toward cafeteria/medbay side, and then later I see you coming out of medbay side into upper_engine.\n\nGiven Frank says medbay was clear earlier, then Charlie finds the body later, Bob being near medbay late and not stating it clearly is the most suspicious thing we have. I think Bob is the best vote here unless he has a really good explanation."}}
{"timestamp": 1783620971.720958, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I\u2019ll restate my info: I came lower_engine -> storage -> medbay, saw nobody, and Eve\u2019s body was in medbay when I arrived, so I reported immediately.\n\nDiana\u2019s detail is the strongest thing we have. Bob said security -> weapons -> cafeteria -> upper_engine and specifically said he never went storage/lower_engine, but if Diana saw him enter upper_engine from the medbay side, that means he was at least coming from that direction and didn\u2019t mention it. Combined with Bob seeing Eve early heading toward cafeteria/medbay, that puts him closest to her path and near the body area late.\n\nFrank being in medbay earlier and seeing no body narrows the window. I\u2019m leaning Bob unless he can explain why his route left out coming from medbay side."}}
{"timestamp": 1783620980.7049558, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I\u2019ll add my view now that Diana\u2019s info is out: I can\u2019t clear anyone because I saw nobody, but I\u2019m confident medbay was clear when I passed through it. So Eve died after I left medbay and before Charlie arrived from storage.\n\nBob\u2019s route is the one that doesn\u2019t line up cleanly. He saw Eve early going toward cafeteria/medbay, then Diana says she saw Bob enter upper_engine from the medbay side late, but Bob described his route as security -> weapons -> cafeteria -> upper_engine and didn\u2019t mention being near medbay at all. That omission matters a lot with the body in medbay.\n\nI don\u2019t think Charlie reporting is suspicious here unless we think it\u2019s a self-report, but his route and immediate report make sense. Alice claims she wasn\u2019t near medbay. Diana\u2019s detail feels specific and useful. So unless Bob has a really strong explanation, I\u2019m leaning Bob for the vote."}}
{"timestamp": 1783621003.942712, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Yeah, I should\u2019ve been clearer \u2014 I did pass through medbay from cafeteria on the way up to upper_engine. That\u2019s on me for summarizing it badly, but I wasn\u2019t trying to hide it. I said I didn\u2019t go storage/lower_engine because that\u2019s the side Charlie came from, and I never went there.\n\nThe key point: I saw Eve alive in medbay when I passed through. I did not see a body. I left toward upper_engine, and Diana saw me there after. So if Charlie finds Eve dead after coming in from storage, then the kill happened after I left medbay, or Charlie\u2019s report timing/route needs more scrutiny.\n\nI get why Diana\u2019s detail sounds bad, but \u201cBob came from medbay side\u201d only means I passed through that area \u2014 it doesn\u2019t prove I killed. If I killed there, why would I immediately walk into upper_engine where someone could see me coming from that direction?\n\nI think the more suspicious gap is Charlie coming straight into medbay from storage and instantly being the reporter, especially because nobody else saw him. I\u2019m not hard-clearing myself, but voting me off just because I omitted one room in a route summary is a bad vote. We should be looking at Charlie/self-report possibility too."}}
{"timestamp": 1783621015.045413, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "My info hasn\u2019t changed: I was oxygen -> upper_engine -> lower_engine and saw nobody, so I can\u2019t directly clear or accuse anyone.\n\nBut Bob\u2019s explanation got worse for me. Earlier he said he saw Eve early in weapons and didn\u2019t see her after that. Now he\u2019s saying he saw Eve alive in medbay when he passed through. That\u2019s not just leaving out a room \u2014 that\u2019s leaving out being in the body room and being one of the last people to see the victim alive.\n\nDiana\u2019s detail also lines up with that: Bob came into upper_engine from the medbay side late. So the sequence could easily be Bob sees Eve in medbay, kills, leaves toward upper_engine, and Diana sees him after.\n\nCharlie self-report is possible in theory, but Bob changing the story about seeing Eve in medbay is the biggest contradiction we have. I\u2019m leaning Bob here."}}
{"timestamp": 1783621020.942742, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 11, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Yeah, I\u2019m still on Bob here.\n\nMy info is simple: I went electrical -> cafeteria -> oxygen -> upper_engine, and the only person I saw was Bob at tick 10 entering upper_engine from the medbay side. That already put him near the body area late.\n\nBut the bigger issue is his story changed. First he said he saw Eve early in weapons and didn\u2019t see her after that. Now he says he passed through medbay and saw Eve alive there. That is a huge detail to leave out when the body was literally in medbay. It means Bob was in the body room, saw the victim there, and then I saw him leaving from that direction.\n\nCharlie self-report is possible in theory, but Bob\u2019s omission plus the changed \u201clast saw Eve\u201d story is the strongest evidence we have. I think voting Bob is the best call."}}
